<title>GREECE: ALPHA CREDIT BANK SETS PRIME RATE FOR YEN LOANS AT 2.55PCT.</title>
<headline>ALPHA CREDIT BANK SETS PRIME RATE FOR YEN LOANS AT 2.55PCT.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-05-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Greece's Alpha Credit Bank</p>
<p>set its prime rate for yen denominated loans at 2.55</p>
<p>percent effective today, it said in a statement.</p>
<p>Prime rates on Alpha's foreign currency loans (Alpha 605</p>
<p>account) will be:</p>
<p>    Yen	    :  2.55 percent</p>
<p>    US Dollars   :  7.70 percent</p>
<p>    Swiss franc  :  3.70 percent</p>
<p>    Mark	   :  5.15 percent</p>
<p>    Ecu	    :  6.15 percent</p>
<p>Alpha Credit Bank said the maximum add-on would be 4.5</p>
<p>percent.</p>
<p>--Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
